From d92e82185ad6648cca5e7f3924d4329b36911cd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:51:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] src: build against Qt 4.8 without changing behaviour on
 Qt 5/6

Signals and slots: every pointer-to-member connect(), QTimer::singleShot()
and QMetaObject::invokeMethod() now uses the SIGNAL()/SLOT() string form,
which Qt 4, 5 and 6 all accept; every lambda slot became a named private
slot (captured values travel through QAction::setData(), a dynamic property
read back from sender(), or Q_ARG()). SingleApplication keeps its
per-connection read buffers in a QHash keyed by the accepted socket instead
of in captured shared pointers, and narrows the socket to its owner with
QFile::setPermissions() where Qt4 has no QLocalServer::setSocketOptions().
The threaded grep in ImitatePass uses FunctorThread and publishes its
results through a queued invokeMethod() with a registered GrepResults
metatype. Qt4 signals are protected, so ConfigDialog asks MainWindow to emit
passGitInitNeeded() through a public requestPassGitInit().

Qt5-only members get an all-version spelling where one exists (constFirst,
chopped, back, cbegin, join(QChar), *SecsSinceEpoch, the static
QFileInfo::exists(), toHtmlEscaped via htmlEscaped()) and a guarded Qt4
fallback otherwise (setResizeMode, setFilterRegExp, QFormLayout row removal,
QDir::removeRecursively, QFontDatabase::systemFont, QLineEdit inline action
/ clear button, QDesktopWidget instead of QScreen, QUrl::fromEncoded for
otpauth URIs, QGuiApplication::setDesktopFileName, and QThread::msleep()
through a subclass because it is protected before Qt 5). The two Qt5-only
.ui properties moved into code under version guards. StoreModel's Qt5-only
virtuals drop `override` on Qt4 and mirror the drag actions with
setSupportedDragActions().

Behavioural differences of Qt4 that surfaced in the test suite: a
signal-killed process reports exit code 0 (now mapped to -1 in Executor),
QDebug appends a trailing space to qWarning() output (printf form used), and
Qt4's global QProcessManager is destroyed before exit-time statics, so the
Pass backends are now destroyed from a qAddPostRoutine() instead of a static
QScopedPointer, which deadlocked ~QProcess() at exit.

